            <ArticleTitle>Squamous cell carcinoma of ascending colon. A case study.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>190-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report here a case of squamous cell carcinoma of Ascending colon occurring in a 58 year old male. Squamous cell carcinomas are known to occur in the Ano rectum frequently, but are extremely rare in colon especially the right colon.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
